  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Wednesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Showers and thunderstorms are \ncontinuing across the forecast area today. The strongest storms \nare expected to be along the Nevada and Oregon/Idaho border and a \nfew of them may become severe, although the strongest storms are \nexpected to remain north of the coverage area. Storms are expected\nto die down after sunset before amplifying again tomorrow, \nalthough still remaining weaker than those expected today. Gusty \nwinds also continue to be a factor, with Wind Advisories still in \neffect for portions of the forecast area. The low pressure center \nthat\u2019s been driving our weather recently will get absorbed back \ninto the broader pattern Friday night, exiting to the east but a \nshortwave trough following right behind it will spark a few final \nshowers in eastern Nevada for Saturday. Zonal flow is expected to \nbuild in behind the shortwave, allowing for dry and warming \nconditions through the end of the forecast. Daytime temperatures \nbegin in the 50s and 60s for Saturday and are expected to reach \nthe mid 80s by Wednesday. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in continuing\nunsettled and wet weather today and tomorrow. Moderate confidence\nin showers on Saturday. Moderate confidence in zonal flow to start\nnext week but high confidence that zonal flow would result in dry\nand warming conditions. No adjustments made to base NBM output.",
